  "findings": [
    "After a cluster rearrangement single trajectories are not reproducible under tiny perturbations: a +1 nm shift of the whole cluster (cache field) diverges more than switching cache to direct (median bubble difference at 0.2 s 6.5 um vs 4.7 um; aspect ratio 2.30 and 2.21 vs 1.34). Trajectory-wise equality of the two field modes cannot be tested beyond such events; deformation comparisons (and world-model targets) must be statistical."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Same homogeneous-water disc model as the cache: no PDMS, wall or end reflections; field shape and the on-axis Y null are model features, not measured.",
    "Frequencies remain 2.4/2.5/2.6 MHz (APECSS response tables); 5 and 10 MHz orders are verified for the field only.",
    "Quadrature verified on random points with |x| < 16 mm and r < 0.75 mm of this geometry; another geometry or points within 0.25 mm of the X discs need a new check.",
